<title>USA: Burlington, Vt seeks to avoid property tax hike.</title>
<headline>Burlington, Vt seeks to avoid property tax hike.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The mayor of Burlington, Vermont, does not plan to ask property owners for a tax increase in 1998.</p>
<p>Peter Clavelle on Thursday plans to discuss his budget, which includes a $450,000 rise in spending, at a public hearing.</p>
<p>But Clavelle says the new capital improvement borrowing limit will help offset that increase. The budget goes to the city council on Monday.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
